This file is only the instructions. The real password file is
toolchain/secrets/pg_pw.txt, which compose.yaml mounts as the secret pg_pw
and which Git ignores (.gitignore: toolchain/secrets/* except *.example).

Create it once, on the Box, in WSL2, from the toolchain folder:

    umask 077
    mkdir -p secrets
    openssl rand -base64 32 | tr -d '\n' > secrets/pg_pw.txt
    chmod 600 secrets/pg_pw.txt

The file holds the password and nothing else (no newline, no "KEY=").
Applications that connect to pgvector read the same file; never copy the
value into compose.yaml, .env, a script or a notebook. To rotate it, change
the password in PostgreSQL (ALTER ROLE postgres PASSWORD ...), then rewrite
the file and restart the services that use it.

